{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/17194-werewolf-one-shot","id":17194,"title":"Werewolf One Shot","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-24T11:32:06-08:00","id":17194,"title":"Werewolf One Shot","content":"So I'm planning a one-shot adventure for a pack of three players that will introduce them to WtF and see if I can get them hooked. But due to my own relative inexperience with running Werewolf I decided that I should throw out my idea here and see if there is anything that a more trained eye would consider that's not working with WtF or looks like a big plot hole.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Background</u></b><br /> <br /> Idea is that the pack is relatively new, hence starting characters, and has a territory that consists of a neighborhood on the outskirts of our own city and a large piece of the rural area outside of it. For the latest time they've been occupied with something which has kept them fairly busy, I'm thinking that a Hunters in Darkness pack has given them some prods them to see if they can't just take a nice slice out of the PC pack's territory. This would explain why they've been both distracted for their urban territory.<br /> <br /> So after successfully standing up to their neighbors the pack returns to the city and finds an unpleasant surprise. Before they left and during the beginning of their clash with the HiD, a gang war was fought between the two gangs in the neighborhood where Gang 1* was driven almost to complete destruction. But after their defeat a man approached the remnants of Gang 1 and took control over it, since then called the Witch Man. He has used rituals to bind spirits to him and bind them to some of the gang's members, both as Urged and a few fully fledged Claimed. Armed with these new powers and their new leader, Gang 1 returned with a vengeance to take on Gang 2 and drive them back.. They gained plenty of new recruits, much thanks to the use of spirits, and people from Gang 2 wanting to join the winning side of the mysterious Witch Man.<br /> <br /> As Gang 1 is gaining greater momentum the pack must take on this great threat to the balance between the worlds, defeat the sorcerer and free or deal with the spirits that are bound in his service. One of my players complain that I don't give them enough of a challenge when I GM but I hope that this will be a change to that. <br /> <br /> * I've yet to come up with names for the gangs, so suggestions are welcome, although I figure that after the change in leadership Gang 1 will probably change name, symbolism etc. into something Norse themed<br /> <br /> ** While I was tempted I have decided against this man being an Awakened Mage due to me not wanting to force myself into using two rule sets. Rather I'm thinking that he is a kind of hedge wizard using rituals to manipulate and control the spirits although he himself has little enough real knowledge about the spirit world and how spirits actually work. If that would make sense and could work. Thus if left alone he could accidentally manage to do something really, really stupid beyond what he's already doing.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Scenario</u></b><br /> <br /> Consolidating their grip on the area and making some last pushes against Gang 2, Gang 1 is spread out in minor groups although in their &quot;base&quot; their leader surrounds himself with a number of armed goons, which should hopefully make a frontal attack less than likely to succeed and inspire the PCs to some other course of action. Not to mention the spiritual protection that the Witch Man has gained from the gang's own spirit.<br /> <br /> Gangbangers from Gang 1 can be encountered pretty much almost anywhere during night time and they are forcing people to pay protection money, silence witnesses, settling grievances, selling drugs, organizing prostitution and so on to establish their control and gain a profit. The PCs should have plenty of opportunities to find gang members and engage them in battle if they would want to thin the ranks or gain information although they will soon start to walk in larger groups and look for a target when they notice that their people are getting killed or disappear. And both their leader as well as the Claimed will not be opposed to the idea of werewolves being behind it.<br /> <br /> Gang 1 consists of the following, and the name in my native language as well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>The Witch Man</b> (H\u00e4xmannen) - a man appearing in his middle age who've got fed up with being poor and downtrodden and so decided to use his forbidden lore for improving his situation. I'm thinking about letting him using some kind of rune magic in the belief that he summons creatures like the Valkyries, Norse elves or the spirits of slain warriors who guides his men rather than actually knowing for sure what he's actually doing with his rituals<br /> <br /> <b>Blackcloak</b> (Svartrocken) - a Claimed former gangster wearing a large black cloak and ski mask to conceal his changes wrought by a violence spirit and is a kind of brutality PR specialist for the gang<br /> <br /> <b>Tail</b> (Svansen) - a gangster Claimed by a loyalty spirit who acts as the Witch Man's body guard <br /> <br /> <b>??? - </b>additional Claimed members, although I haven't decided what kind of spirits might have Claimed them, what to call them etc.<br /> <br /> Lots of Urged and un-Ridden members armed with lighter fire arms, knives, baseball bats, crowbars etc. and a few heavier pieces. Probably around 40-50 of them, or possibly even more.<br /> The gang's spirit, who is delighted with the increase in power that the Witch Man has accomplished for it. No idea for names, powers, bans etc. for it yet<br /> <br /> Gang 2 is almost finished and can probably muster little more than maybe around 5-7 really scared guys who are more interested in getting out of the city than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T03:59:22-08:00","id":17645,"title":"","content":"Looks good to me!<br /> <br /> Ideas:<br /> <br /> Gang 1 is controlled not by a host of smaller spirits but by one single larger spirit that's basically urging all of its members at the same time. Something like a collective conscious that's connecting them. Go scary and weird.<br /> <br /> Gang 1 is, by virtue of having destroyed the power base of Gang 2, actually making the city a safer place for everyone. That doesn't mean it's a good idea to let a huge spirit Urge a whole lot of people.<br /> <br /> Gang 1 absolutely tries to recruit the PCs, because hey, they're in power, and they have all the money, cool cars, hot babes, and wouldn't you want to be part of that? Some NPC werewolves in town gladly join Gang 1.<br /> <br /> Blackcloack is Claimed by a traitor spirit - he's supportive of Gang 1 right now, but he'll eventually bite the hand that feeds him. He's the weak link of Gang 1 - it's only a matter of time until he turns traitor and assists the PC. A skilled Ithaeur PC might pick up the clues and figure that out by himself.<br /> And, of course, Blackcloak will also betray the PCs as well, because it's in his nature to never be loyal.<br /> <br /> The spirit behind Gang 1 used to be the pack totem of the Hunter in Darkness pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T10:56:30-08:00","id":19265,"title":"","content":"Thanks Christian A!<br /> <br /> I consider you a kind of Werewolf guru on the forums so reading this means some. And thanks for the ideas you posted. They've helped me to refine a few things. And I really like the idea of having Blackcloak be claimed by a traitor spirit, although odds are that it will go straight over my players' heads. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I am considering having the Witch Man make a deal with a stronger Crime Spirit and use its brood to strengthen his gang with Ridden gangbangers. I wanted to keep the Witch Man as the initially central antagonist and so this spirit will take the backseat until the Witch Man asks for stronger help towards the strange creatures that are assailing him and his gang. This brood should together with the stronger spirit also ensure that the pack can't just waltz through the Hisil and kill the gangbangers as they want.And this would ensure that the spirits claiming gang members are fits the theme nicely.<br /> <br /> All other comments and ideas are welcome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T12:33:47-08:00","id":19311,"title":"","content":"Here's a theme that I particularly like to emphasize: spirits don't happen in a vacuum. The Shadow is a reflection of the Flesh, right? A crime spirit doesn't just spring into existence - a stronger crime spirit needed some sort of catalyst that created it and that made it so powerful.<br /> <br /> Ask yourself the question, then - why is the crime spirit so powerful? Which events in the Flesh granted it its power?<br /> <br /> Also - what are you doing with Gang 2? What's their particular role in the story? I feel I don't quite understand their purpose in the story as of yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T08:14:25-08:00","id":19748,"title":"","content":"I totally agree that the Shadow and the Flesh are tied together.<br /> <br /> In regards to the strong crime spirit I figured that with two gangs, and in real life this neighborhood is considered a bit shady, and their operations they would create enough resonance within the Shadow to justify this powerful crime spirit. As I see it the are has been this way for decades and with gangs running stuff I figured it would be a good justification for why the spirit is there. It has probably been pretty much tied to the gangs to feed of their activities but when the Witch Man came into contact with it, it jumped for the chance to gain more essence. <br /> <br /> As for Gang 2 I have no real idea. They are kind of mostly there to explain why the Witch Man could take over Gang 1 and why the trouble started now and not before, or was noticed by the werewolves. If you've got ideas I'm all eager to hear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T12:55:38-08:00","id":19865,"title":"","content":"Hm ..<br /> <br /> crime stories often feature escalation, right? You bring knives, they bring guns, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> So if Gang 1 is assisted by a host of spirits, what if maybe Gang 2 will eventually be found by a cult of Fire-Touched, who give them hope, faith and a cause to believe in (and guns, and hate and all the usual Fire-Touched madness). This also makes the entire situation less binary (PCs vs. Gang 1).<br /> <br /> You can always substitute other antagonists. Desperate time call for desperate measure and imprudent deals, right? Have Gang 2 bring in the Azlu or Beshilu (definitely my favourite Werewolf antagonists!). Turn them into a cult of sin under the command of a Bale Hound. Have one of them be wolfblooded and in league with a rival Forsaken pack.<br /> <br /> Alternately - the leader of Gang 2 undergoes his First Change as a Rahu. Give the PCs a chance to educate him on the ways of the Forsaken and win allies.<br /> <br /> Hell, you could even use the First Change hook on gang 1 - a human, non-Claimed member of Gang 1 experiences the First Change. The H\u00e4xmannen wants him on his side, of course. It's up to the PCs to show him what being Forsaken is all about and why creatures/things like the H\u00e4xmannen are bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-29T09:52:26-08:00","id":20228,"title":"","content":"Its a pretty cool idea to bring the Pure into the mix and let them have a go at the pack's territory with Gang 2 as expandable pawns, or create one of the Uratha from Gang 2. The issue is of course that this is supposed to be a one-shot session and thus that kind of plot probably isn't needed and I wanted to focus on the core of the Uratha duties, the aspect of the Shadow and how both humans and spirits can mess up the &quot;balance&quot; between the two. But if they want to continue to play Werewolf then I'll definitely going to keep these ideas for further use. Could also turn it into a race to see if the pack or the Pure will catch the young werewolf first. <br /> <br /> As for other werewolves I've also given the present situation with packs and such some thought and came up with this, if my players would like to know how the situation looks. And I know about the names but I didn't have any inspiration at that point.<br /> <br /> Forsaken<br /> <br /> Rural<br /> <br /> F Pack 1 - having their territory to the west of the town and so have some border in common with the PC pack <br /> 2 Hunters in Darkness, 1 Bone Shadow<br /> <br /> F Pack 2 - having its territory a couple of miles south of the city where they clash with P Pack 1 on an almost regular basis, they have a fairly extended territory although they can't exactly be described a friends of humanity or at least of urban folks<br /> 2 Hunters in Darkness, 1 Blood Talon, 1 Storm Lady<br /> <br /> Urban <br /> <br /> F Pack 3 - has its territory in the eastern parts of town and stretching out into the wilderness<br /> 2 Iron Masters, 1 Bone Shadow, 1 Blood Talon<br /> <br /> F Pack 4 - its territory lies in the central town and borders with the PC pack, it was this pack that gave the PC pack part of its territory because they found themselves unable to hold it anyway. They are the pack mostly involved with fighting the local Pure in the town, namely in P Pack 2<br /> 1 Iron Mistress, 2 Blood Talons, 1 Storm Lord<br /> <br /> PC Pack - three young werewolves of unknown Tribe and Auspice<br /> <br /> The local elders consists of a Blood Talon from F Pack 4 and a Huntress in Darkness from F Pack 2 and these are considered fonts of wisdom in regards to things concerning the Uratha by the local Forsaken, as well as dealing with life in rural and urban environment respectively<br /> <br /> Pure<br /> <br /> Rural<br /> <br /> P Pack 1 - several miles to the south from where they are struggle to drive out and if possibly kill F Pack 2, they are a terror in the forests south of town<br /> 5 Predator Kings<br /> <br /> Urban<br /> <br /> P Pack 2 - have its territory in the southern parts of the town<br /> 4 Fire-touched, 2 Ivory Claws<br /> <br /> P Pack 3 - hangs on the southern-eastern parts of the town <br /> 3 Fire Touched<br /> <br /> As for the humans, I figure that the police is extremely corrupt while I'm going to play up both how segregated the town is and how violent it is. So a really dark world to make things be more explainable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T11:23:48-07:00","id":110189,"title":"","content":"Ok, the game went pretty well although I did have to fudge the rolls somewhat when the pack of two, they lost the NPC in an earlier battle, walked straight into an ambush with close to a dozen or so Claimed and H\u00e4xmannen himself. They would probably have died there had I not fudged the die, and for that I get some mocking for being to soft on them. But no more! This time I'm gunning for at least one PC kill.<br /> <br /> Anyway the situation is as follows; H\u00e4xmannen and his gang are destroyed at the loss of the Bone Shadow Jacob (mercilessly mocked as &quot;Twilight&quot;) and some degree of collateral damage. The pack also made a deal with a spirit lord of crime to ensure crime levels in the territory is up in exchange for the spirits neutrality in the war with H\u00e4xmannen, while the spirit of the neighborhood itself hates their guts.<br /> <br /> The interesting thing now is that while the PCs have a territory neither of them speaks the First Tongue and neither of them are skilled in Occult matters and so deal with the spirits is likely to come down to beating the crap out of them and hope they get the picture. Needless to say this will probably hold for a short time before someone comes along to manipulate these spirits and cause some real hell for the PCs, if not an entire local choir of spirits decides to just kill these half-breeds right now. To this the great use of violence and mass of people affected by Lunacy has caused a multitude of violence, murder, blood and madness spirits to cross from the Shadow into the territory by the unguarded Loci.<br /> <br /> One the characters is starting up his own gang to run a criminal empire. To this three families of wolf-blooded have moved into the territory at the urging of the Uratha to get some degree of protection from the parts of town where they are at risk from the Pure. But while this might look like good to the PCs there's of course some problem. First an Azlu has silently infiltrated the territory with the intention of weaving its webs around the local Loci and at the same time a pack of Suthanu-sua (werecats) have made it into the territory with the assumtion of destroying the gangs who previously made life a hell for the denizens. What the Suthanu-sua finds instead are the two Uratha and their new gang who have a fairly good chance to make these critters attack them.<br /> <br /> So between the lack of a shaman, an invasion of murder-inclined spirits, an Azlu and the werecats, how will two werewolves hold on to their territory? We'll probably going to find out very fairly soon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I imagine that the theme of this meeting will be; &quot;hunted hunters&quot; as the Uratha hunts the spirits and are in turn hunted by the Azlu and the werecats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T12:55:27-07:00","id":111006,"title":"","content":"Looks good. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T14:22:58-07:00","id":111047,"title":"","content":"Just remember the rule of thumb that total party wipeouts are bad...but killing half of them is totally legit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> One thing I would heavily suggest in a scenario such as this is don't railroad your players by making only the option you planned for the only option. If the players think of an extremely creative way to resolve the situation or turn it in their favor, improvisation may be necessary, but the players tend to enjoy it more. This is mostly because it was their brainchild and seeing you run along with it gives them faith that you are playing the game for them, not playing the game for you.<br /> <br /> It also sets the stage for the future when only a single solution may be the only answer. If they know that you generally run with good ideas, but this time you are not, they won't hold it against you.<br /> <br /> For example, in the situation you described above, if the players make contact with the Azlu, they may decide that its gauntlet strengthening abilities are a valuable tool right now and let it go about its business. By doing so, it helps keep the spirits out of the territory so they can concentrate on the werecats. This turn it into a 1v1 fight almost rather than a 1v3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T00:14:00-07:00","id":111939,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Good point to avoid railroading. I can totally see the pack making some kind of deal with the werecats and/or with the Azlu in order to stablize the territory. Hell, they can even make it a simple fix to just fight off the spirits, although they will eventually want to do something about the Azlu...after its have had a chance to grow. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In regards to what will come after that I'm thinking of testing the pack against a pack of four young Fire-Touched and see how they go with that. But that's a thing for the future and I may have to put it up another session or two.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}